From 0ef35dfa3fd259e99def0393a9171469a501d136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:22:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/20] hw/misc: add i.MX6 GPMI NAND controller model (APBH DMA
 + BCH)

Models the NAND subsystem at the register level the stock software
drives it through, backed by a flat de-ECC'd page image (page N at
offset N*2048, BCH treated as error-free):

- APBH: CTRL0 SFTRST/CLKGATE latches, per-channel IRQ enable/status,
  CHANNEL_CTRL channel resets, 4 channels with the 16-byte register
  groups (CURCMDAR/NXTCMDAR/CMD/BAR/SEMA at 0x100 + n*0x70), and a
  synchronous mxs-style descriptor engine (12-byte hardware command
  + inline PIO words forwarded to consecutive GPMI registers).
- GPMI: CTRL0/1, ECCCTRL, PAYLOAD/AUXILIARY, STAT; a raw-NAND chip
  state machine (reset, READID, status, page read/program/erase with
  CLE+INCREMENT command/address byte encoding).
- BCH: pass-through decode/encode into the payload/auxiliary buffers,
  COMPLETE_IRQ semantics; layout registers are stored and used for
  the auxiliary status layout.

Boots the stock U-Boot 2014.04 through its full startup cycle: probe,
environment, bootcmd with UBI mount attempts and the unlocked/normal
boot decision logic. The chip identity probe still returns no device
(next task); all other paths run.

Verified with the gen3 NAND dump repacked as a logical image.
